{"units": [{"id": "mvp-comment-212-2-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ is found constructed in both ways: ⟦2⟧ (⟦3⟧. 503), and ⟦4⟧ ⟦5⟧ (⟦6⟧). Schütz changes the first ⟦7⟧ to ⟦8⟧ (cf. above 473), but is ⟦9⟧ factually correct? It seems better, with H. L. Ahrens, to change the second ⟦10⟧ to ⟦11⟧ (cf. 39. 170. 180), and then to adopt ⟦12⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-212-2-mentioned1", "translation": "of the hearth"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-212-2-mentioned2", "translation": "the hearth of your house"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-212-2-mentioned3", "translation": "houses with hearths"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-212-2-mentioned4", "translation": "of the house"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-212-2-mentioned5", "translation": "by custom"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-212-2-mentioned6", "translation": "is at the hearth"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-212-2-mentioned7", "translation": "of the house"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-212-2-mentioned8", "translation": "of the inner chambers"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-212-2-mentioned9", "translation": "of the hearths"}]}